From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Karl Godard <karl@minimal.dev>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 19:22:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] virtio/vsock: refuse a stream whose host unix leg cannot be
 established

When the guest opens a stream to a vsock port mapped to a host unix
socket with krun_add_vsock_port2(..., listen=false), process_op_request()
creates the host leg with UnixProxy::new(...).unwrap() and then connects
it. Both steps can fail on the host, and neither failure reached the
guest as a refusal:

- UnixProxy::new() fails when socket(AF_UNIX) fails (EMFILE, ENFILE,
  ENOBUFS, ENOMEM), a transient host condition. The unwrap() turned it
  into a panic on the event-manager thread, which aborted the whole VMM.
- UnixProxy::connect() fails when nothing listens at the path (ENOENT,
  ECONNREFUSED) or the backlog is full (EAGAIN). The proxy stays Idle and
  is never polled, yet confirm_connect() still sent OP_RESPONSE and the
  proxy was inserted into the map. The guest's connect() succeeded into a
  connection that never carries data.

Refuse the connection in both cases instead: log the error and answer
the guest with OP_RST, the reply the function already sends when a guest
connects to a port that is mapped for listening. Nothing is inserted into
the proxy map, so there is no state to clean up, and the guest's connect()
fails with ECONNRESET while the VM keeps running.

Also answer OP_RST when the guest connects to a port that has no unix
mapping at all. That request used to be dropped, so the guest waited out
its connect timeout.

Upstream: https://github.com/libkrun/libkrun/pull/915
Signed-off-by: Karl Godard <karl@minimal.dev>
Assisted-by: Claude Code: claude-opus-5-5
---
 src/devices/src/virtio/vsock/muxer.rs | 44 ++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 40 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/devices/src/virtio/vsock/muxer.rs b/src/devices/src/virtio/vsock/muxer.rs
index 6cf8b6f..2a8a68e 100644
--- a/src/devices/src/virtio/vsock/muxer.rs
+++ b/src/devices/src/virtio/vsock/muxer.rs
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@ use super::defs::uapi;
 use super::muxer_rxq::{rx_to_pkt, MuxerRxQ};
 use super::muxer_thread::MuxerThread;
 use super::packet::{TsiConnectReq, TsiGetnameRsp, VsockPacket};
-use super::proxy::{Proxy, ProxyRemoval, ProxyUpdate};
+use super::proxy::{Proxy, ProxyRemoval, ProxyStatus, ProxyUpdate};
 use super::reaper::ReaperThread;
 #[cfg(target_os = "macos")]
 use super::timesync::TimesyncThread;
@@ -560,7 +560,7 @@ impl VsockMuxer {
                 }
                 let rxq = self.rxq.clone();
 
-                let mut unix = UnixProxy::new(
+                let mut unix = match UnixProxy::new(
                     id,
                     self.cid,
                     pkt.dst_port(),
@@ -569,16 +569,52 @@ impl VsockMuxer {
                     queue.clone(),
                     rxq,
                     path.to_path_buf(),
-                )
-                .unwrap();
+                ) {
+                    Ok(unix) => unix,
+                    Err(e) => {
+                        error!(
+                            "error creating unix proxy for port {}, sending rst: {e}",
+                            pkt.dst_port()
+                        );
+                        self.push_packet(MuxerRx::Reset {
+                            local_port: pkt.dst_port(),
+                            peer_port: pkt.src_port(),
+                        });
+                        return;
+                    }
+                };
                 let tsi = TsiConnectReq {
                     peer_port: 0,
                     addr: SocketAddrV4::new(Ipv4Addr::new(0, 0, 0, 0), 0).into(),
                 };
                 let update = unix.connect(pkt, tsi);
+                if !matches!(
+                    unix.status(),
+                    ProxyStatus::Connected | ProxyStatus::Connecting
+                ) {
+                    error!(
+                        "error connecting unix proxy for port {} to {}, sending rst",
+                        pkt.dst_port(),
+                        path.display()
+                    );
+                    self.push_packet(MuxerRx::Reset {
+                        local_port: pkt.dst_port(),
+                        peer_port: pkt.src_port(),
+                    });
+                    return;
+                }
                 unix.confirm_connect(pkt);
                 proxy_map.insert(id, Mutex::new(Box::new(unix)));
                 self.process_proxy_update(id, update);
+            } else {
+                debug!(
+                    "no unix socket mapped for port {}, sending rst",
+                    pkt.dst_port()
+                );
+                self.push_packet(MuxerRx::Reset {
+                    local_port: pkt.dst_port(),
+                    peer_port: pkt.src_port(),
+                });
             }
         }
     }
